===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*sehs}}, whence also {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{m|ofs|sex}}, {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|sehs}}, {{etyl|dum|-}} {{m|dum|sesse}} ({{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|zes}}), {{etyl|goh|-}} {{m|goh|sehs}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{m|de|sechs}}), {{etyl|non|-}} {{m|non|sex}} ({{etyl|sv|-}} {{m|sv|sex}}), {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐍃𐌰𐌹𐌷𐍃}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*swéḱs}}, cognate with {{etyl|grc|-}} {{m|grc|ἕξ}}, {{etyl|la|-}} {{m|la|sex}}, {{etyl|sga|-}} {{m|sga|se|sē}} ({{etyl|ga|-}} {{m|ga|sé}}), {{etyl|sla-pro|-}} {{m|sla-pro|*šestь}} ({{etyl|ru|-}} {{m|ru|шесть}}).

